scene "OTD4 Dynamics Tour"
unit: cm

# ====== The OTD4 dynamics tour ======
# Six new physics domains, all on the same scene so you can see how they
# read the same parts through different lenses.
#
# 1. aerodynamics   — drag, lift, terminal velocity, Reynolds, Mach
# 2. fluid dynamics — Bernoulli, Poiseuille, Stokes, hydrostatic pressure
# 3. electrodynamics — Ohm, Kirchhoff, RC/RL/LC, Maxwell's light
# 4. stellar dynamics — N-body, virial theorem, Jeans scale
# 5. rigid body dynamics — inertia tensor, angular momentum, gyroscopes
# 6. magnetism (already in OTD3, now with magnetize: keyword)
#
# The parts are spread out enough that strict-overlap passes.

# --- the parts: a wing, a wire, a spinning disk, three lead balls, a water pool ---
wing    = cube(w: 20cm, d: 3cm, h: 1cm) at (0, 5cm, 0) material: aluminum
wire    = cylinder(r: 1mm, h: 20cm) rotate (90deg, 0, 0) at (15cm, 10cm, 0) material: copper
disk    = cylinder(r: 8cm, h: 2cm) at (-25cm, 5cm, 0) material: steel
star_a  = sphere 2cm at (-45cm, 5cm, 0)   material: lead
star_b  = sphere 2cm at (-45cm, 5cm, 8cm) material: lead
star_c  = sphere 2cm at (-37cm, 5cm, 12cm) material: lead
pool    = cube(w: 8cm, d: 8cm, h: 4cm) at (25cm, 2cm, 15cm) material: water

# --- magnetize the disk so it becomes a permanent magnet ---
magnetize: disk

# --- run every new simulation ---
simulate: aero
simulate: fluid
simulate: electro
simulate: stellar
simulate: rigid
simulate: magnet

# --- and the new strict-overlap audit ---
strict: overlap
overlap: check
